w4os-engine on Debian
=====================

The system layout
-----------------

Installing the package makes the account the instances run as (opensim), the folders of the layout, owned by it
through dpkg-statoverride (an administrator's own override is kept), and /etc/w4os/w4os.conf, left as it is
once written (the /etc/opensim/opensim.conf of before w4os is moved there, as it is):

  /etc/w4os             the config of the suite, w4os.conf
  /etc/opensim          the config of OpenSimulator: the grids (grids/<grid>), the enabled instances (robust.d, opensim.d)
  /var/lib/opensim      data, and the home of the account
  /var/log/opensim      logs
  /var/cache/opensim    cache
  /var/backups/opensim  backups

Each OpenSimulator release installed in /usr/share/opensim gets an install profile in w4os.conf, added and
removed with it; the latest one is the default.

The files of a grid
-------------------

Every ini file of a grid may hold a password: it is readable by its owner and the group of the web server only
(mode 640, the group of WebGroup in /etc/w4os/w4os.conf, www-data by default), as the helpers read the settings of the
grid. Each install or upgrade of the package gives them these modes again, and adds the files a grid is missing
(MoneyServer.ini).

The instances run as SystemUser of /etc/w4os/w4os.conf (opensim on a new install; the owner of an install that exists,
taken by opensim import --in-place or a migration). The units of w4os-cli follow it through a drop-in,
/etc/systemd/system/<unit>.d/w4os-system-user.conf, written by each install or upgrade of the package, and by
php /usr/share/w4os-engine/bin/opensim-layout.php (as root) after the account changes.

Purge
-----

Purging the package removes /var/cache/opensim and the owner it gave to the folders of the layout. Config, data,
logs, backups and the account are kept.
